; The lane extracts feed scalar fmuls only, which the backend folds into
; by-element fmuls (fmul d0, d1, v2.d[1]), so the extracts cost nothing in the
; scalar code and their removal saves nothing. Without that credit the
; 2-element part of the fmul reduction with the hoisted gathered operands is
; not profitable: the scalar code is fmul + fmla + fmadd.
